WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.210
Heavy rain last night, and the bridge on

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.590
my usual road to school is under water.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.140
I always drive through Kesi and Mina.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.500
Which way is the shortest now?

5
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.170
Today: the shortest way, and a

6
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.570
sure method to find it.

7
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.450
Draw the problem as a map: places

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.970
are dots, roads are lines, and

9
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.290
each road has its length.

10
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.170
Here there are a home, six

11
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.690
villages and the school.

12
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.190
A way’s length is just its roads added up.

13
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.030
The road through Bora looks the

14
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.910
straightest: five kilometres, then ten.

15
00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.370
That’s fifteen.

16
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.630
The winding way through Tala, Kesi and

17
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:47.210
Mina is four, three, two and four.

18
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.910
That’s only thirteen.

19
00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.630
To be sure, use a method Edsger

20
00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.930
Dijkstra found in nineteen fifty-six.

21
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.100
Every place gets a number: the shortest

22
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.300
way found so far, and home starts at zero.

23
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.130
Each turn, settle the waiting place

24
00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.150
with the smallest number, because

25
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.250
nothing can beat it now.

26
00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.850
Then its roads may lower its

27
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:10.790
neighbours’ numbers.

28
00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.510
From home, the roads give Tala

29
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.750
four, Bora five and Rubi six.

30
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.170
Settle Tala, and Kesi gets seven.

31
00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.650
Settle Bora, then Rubi, then

32
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.970
Kesi, and Mina drops to nine.

33
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.250
Settle Mina, and the school gets thirteen.

34
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.130
Picture water spreading out from your home

35
00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:36.530
along every road at the same speed.

36
00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.330
It reaches the nearest places first.

37
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.420
The first time it reaches the

38
00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.700
school, it came the shortest way.

39
00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:45.490
Quick check!

40
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.680
Bora has five and Kesi has

41
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.060
seven, and both are waiting.

42
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.560
Which do you settle next?

43
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.860
Bora, the smallest number.

44
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.970
Any other way to Bora would pass a place

45
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:04.230
that is already farther, so five is final.

46
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.080
That’s why the method

47
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.380
never has to go back.

48
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.680
Map apps and delivery vans use faster

49
00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.120
versions of it every second.

50
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:16.050
Now flood the bridge between Kesi and

51
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.190
Mina, and run the same method again.

52
00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.000
The shortest way becomes Home, Rubi,

53
00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.240
Sana, School: fourteen kilometres.

54
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.970
The shortest way depends on today’s map,

55
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.670
so plan again when a road closes.

56
00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.750
Every family has its own

57
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.230
shortest way, and some are long.

58
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.440
Before the council builds a

59
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.400
footbridge, the school can measure

60
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.240
each village’s shortest way.

61
00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:47.200
Then ask: whose walk gets shorter, and

62
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.940
who still walks the farthest?

63
00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.430
In the app, find the

64
00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.310
shortest way yourself.

65
00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.160
Tap Home, then always tap the waiting

66
00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.960
village with the smallest number,

67
00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.580
until the school is settled.

68
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.850
Then flood the bridge and

69
00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:02.730
find the new way.

70
00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:04.430
Your turn.

71
00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.520
The road through Bora looks

72
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.800
the straightest of all.

73
00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.010
Is it the shortest way to school?

74
00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.030
No: fifteen kilometres, against

75
00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.230
thirteen through Tala, Kesi and Mina.

76
00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.190
Remember: draw the map with road

77
00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.790
lengths and add them up.

78
00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.600
Settle the smallest waiting number first.

79
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.850
And when a road closes, plan again.

80
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.440
Try it in class tomorrow: chalk a

81
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.980
map on the playground, with

82
00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.020
villages, roads and their lengths.

83
00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.820
Pupils stand on the villages with

84
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:39.560
number cards and settle the

85
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.040
smallest number each turn.

86
00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.920
Then close a road, and find the

87
00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.240
new shortest way together.
